WEBVTT

00:00:00.043 --> 00:00:01.044 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
GridBot Builder.

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.784 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
GridBot Blueprint.

00:00:03.349 --> 00:00:04.113 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson two.

00:00:04.633 --> 00:00:06.141 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
What you are going to need.

00:00:06.952 --> 00:00:08.098 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Education only.

00:00:08.657 --> 00:00:09.971 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Not financial advice.

00:00:10.491 --> 00:00:12.542 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is general information and

00:00:12.542 --> 00:00:14.746 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
doesn't consider your objectives,

00:00:14.746 --> 00:00:16.646 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
financial situation or needs.

00:00:17.166 --> 00:00:18.930 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Crypto is high risk; you could

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:20.621 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lose all the money you put in.

00:00:21.141 --> 00:00:23.206 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Past performance is not a reliable

00:00:23.206 --> 00:00:24.915 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
indicator of future results.

00:00:25.965 --> 00:00:28.022 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The prices are public historical

00:00:28.022 --> 00:00:29.784 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
daily closes, marked Example.

00:00:30.984 --> 00:00:32.883 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
No order is sent from this lesson.

00:00:33.882 --> 00:00:35.763 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Crypto is a digital coin, such

00:00:35.763 --> 00:00:37.566 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
as bitcoin, and a daily close

00:00:37.566 --> 00:00:39.370 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
is the last price of that day.

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:41.986 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A band, also called the range, is

00:00:41.986 --> 00:00:43.999 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the top and the bottom, a gap is

00:00:43.999 --> 00:00:46.180 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the space between two lines, and

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:48.276 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the step is how wide that gap is.

00:00:48.796 --> 00:00:50.812 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stop is the rule for what you will

00:00:50.812 --> 00:00:52.611 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
do if the price leaves the band.

00:00:53.131 --> 00:00:55.031 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Like a packing list before a trip,

00:00:55.031 --> 00:00:56.930 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your page comes before any screen.

00:00:57.854 --> 00:00:59.474 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
By the end you will fill in a

00:00:59.474 --> 00:01:01.302 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
seven-item checklist on paper.

00:01:02.502 --> 00:01:04.792 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You will keep every secret off that page.

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:07.644 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You will mark the page Example so

00:01:07.644 --> 00:01:09.376 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
nobody can read it as an order.

00:01:10.484 --> 00:01:12.882 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The seven items are: a notebook, the

00:01:12.882 --> 00:01:15.279 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
three words from lesson one, range,

00:01:15.279 --> 00:01:17.676 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
levels and stop, the pair, paper or a

00:01:17.676 --> 00:01:20.416 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
demo account, no secrets, a written stop,

00:01:20.416 --> 00:01:22.984 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the word Example on every figure.

00:01:23.504 --> 00:01:24.885 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Each item has a reason.

00:01:25.405 --> 00:01:26.746 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The notebook is the plan

00:01:26.746 --> 00:01:27.863 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you can check later.

00:01:28.116 --> 00:01:29.456 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The three words stop you

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:31.076 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
drawing a grid with no edges.

00:01:31.446 --> 00:01:32.731 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The pair names what you

00:01:32.731 --> 00:01:34.183 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
buy and what you pay with.

00:01:34.558 --> 00:01:36.022 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Paper or a demo is learner

00:01:36.022 --> 00:01:37.556 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
plates, or training wheels.

00:01:38.076 --> 00:01:40.254 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
No secrets keeps the keys off the page.

00:01:40.747 --> 00:01:42.479 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The written stop is the action.

00:01:42.772 --> 00:01:44.560 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Example marks a teaching number.

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:46.479 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
For this course the pair is

00:01:46.479 --> 00:01:48.117 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bitcoin priced in US dollars.

00:01:48.637 --> 00:01:50.830 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A demo account uses pretend money.

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:52.485 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A daily close is the

00:01:52.485 --> 00:01:53.714 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
last price of the day.

00:01:54.211 --> 00:01:55.664 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You are naming that public

00:01:55.664 --> 00:01:57.228 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
series, not choosing an app.

00:01:58.040 --> 00:01:59.772 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Three words, before any number.

00:02:00.177 --> 00:02:02.762 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Range is the top line and the bottom line.

00:02:03.282 --> 00:02:05.306 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An order is an instruction to buy

00:02:05.306 --> 00:02:07.255 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
or sell that can wait for a price.

00:02:07.775 --> 00:02:10.142 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Levels are the price lines where orders

00:02:10.142 --> 00:02:12.320 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
wait, like the rungs of a ladder, and a

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:14.387 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
gap is the space between two of them.

00:02:14.821 --> 00:02:17.167 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stop is the rule for what you will do if

00:02:17.167 --> 00:02:19.573 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a daily close finishes outside the band

00:02:19.573 --> 00:02:22.059 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the next daily close is still outside.

00:02:22.579 --> 00:02:24.399 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The figures from lesson 1 are

00:02:24.399 --> 00:02:26.068 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
on the card, marked Example.

00:02:26.588 --> 00:02:28.599 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If you can only say one of the three

00:02:28.599 --> 00:02:30.499 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
words, the page is missing a part.

00:02:31.369 --> 00:02:33.492 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A wallet is where your crypto is held.

00:02:33.808 --> 00:02:35.372 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A seed phrase is the list of

00:02:35.372 --> 00:02:37.115 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
words that unlocks that wallet.

00:02:37.635 --> 00:02:39.031 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A private key is a secret

00:02:39.031 --> 00:02:40.498 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that can move your crypto.

00:02:41.018 --> 00:02:43.347 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An API secret is a password that lets

00:02:43.347 --> 00:02:45.677 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a program place orders on an account.

00:02:46.197 --> 00:02:48.824 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You never type a seed phrase, a private

00:02:48.824 --> 00:02:51.196 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
key, or an API secret onto this page.

00:02:51.716 --> 00:02:53.515 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The chart has no balance on it.

00:02:54.035 --> 00:02:55.990 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A public close is not your account.

00:02:56.466 --> 00:02:58.096 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a form asks for a secret,

00:02:58.096 --> 00:02:59.882 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that form is not this lesson.

00:03:00.932 --> 00:03:02.503 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You copy the band onto the

00:03:02.503 --> 00:03:04.223 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
page, not every day's prices.

00:03:04.743 --> 00:03:06.977 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Copy the bottom line and the top

00:03:06.977 --> 00:03:09.125 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
line, with six gaps of about 900.

00:03:09.645 --> 00:03:11.098 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Every close in that window

00:03:11.098 --> 00:03:12.383 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
stayed inside the band.

00:03:12.927 --> 00:03:14.330 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Mark each figure Example.

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:16.919 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Worked check: pair, band,

00:03:16.919 --> 00:03:18.377 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
gaps, stop, and Example.

00:03:18.897 --> 00:03:20.964 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the stop line is only a tick with

00:03:20.964 --> 00:03:23.178 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
no sentence, the page fails the check.

00:03:23.698 --> 00:03:25.471 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The rule has to say: if a daily

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:27.553 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
close finishes outside the band

00:03:27.553 --> 00:03:29.634 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the next daily close is still

00:03:29.634 --> 00:03:31.407 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
outside, the example is over.

00:03:32.457 --> 00:03:34.468 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A page is the notebook you can hold.

00:03:34.964 --> 00:03:36.925 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An exchange is the app or website

00:03:36.925 --> 00:03:38.886 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
where people buy and sell crypto.

00:03:39.406 --> 00:03:40.915 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The screen is the exchange.

00:03:41.345 --> 00:03:42.868 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson 1 ended by asking

00:03:42.868 --> 00:03:44.163 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you to bring the page.

00:03:44.683 --> 00:03:46.079 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This lesson is that page.

00:03:46.594 --> 00:03:48.605 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Open the notebook before any screen.

00:03:49.516 --> 00:03:51.583 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write today's date on the first line.

00:03:51.932 --> 00:03:53.776 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Under it, write the word Example.

00:03:54.159 --> 00:03:55.638 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Example means a real past

00:03:55.638 --> 00:03:57.046 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
price used for practice.

00:03:57.566 --> 00:03:59.689 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is not an order and not a forecast.

00:04:00.814 --> 00:04:01.987 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write the pair first.

00:04:02.391 --> 00:04:03.788 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The base is what you buy.

00:04:04.288 --> 00:04:06.020 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The quote is what you pay with.

00:04:06.354 --> 00:04:09.313 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
For this course the prices are the summer

00:04:09.313 --> 00:04:11.750 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bitcoin closes, so you buy the base,

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:14.447 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bitcoin, with the quote, US dollars, and

00:04:14.447 --> 00:04:16.536 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that row is labelled BTC/USD.

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:19.067 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Every other row depends on the pair.

00:04:19.273 --> 00:04:21.449 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a fee sum is in Australian

00:04:21.449 --> 00:04:23.625 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollars, that sum goes on its

00:04:23.625 --> 00:04:25.706 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
own line, labelled BTC/AUD.

00:04:26.226 --> 00:04:28.285 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Do not put a US dollar price and an

00:04:28.285 --> 00:04:30.649 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Australian dollar fee on the same row.

00:04:31.169 --> 00:04:33.459 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Do not mix the two currencies on one row.

00:04:34.454 --> 00:04:37.039 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Range is the top line and the bottom line.

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:40.673 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
On the summer chart those

00:04:41.018 --> 00:04:44.251 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lines are 24,930 and 30,331.

00:04:44.771 --> 00:04:46.168 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Both figures are Example.

00:04:46.671 --> 00:04:48.571 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Levels are the lines between them.

00:04:48.861 --> 00:04:51.020 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Six gaps of about 900 dollars sit

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:53.018 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
between the top and the bottom.

00:04:53.538 --> 00:04:55.394 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write the top and the bottom only

00:04:55.394 --> 00:04:57.405 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
after you have said what a range is.

00:04:57.838 --> 00:04:59.728 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then write one gap, and how you

00:04:59.728 --> 00:05:01.697 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
got it: the top minus the bottom,

00:05:01.697 --> 00:05:03.586 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
divided by the number of gaps.

00:05:04.636 --> 00:05:06.048 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The stop sentence has to

00:05:06.048 --> 00:05:07.221 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
say what you will do.

00:05:07.698 --> 00:05:09.731 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A bot is a program that places and

00:05:09.731 --> 00:05:11.915 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
cancels the waiting orders for you.

00:05:12.435 --> 00:05:14.446 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Two daily closes outside the band,

00:05:14.446 --> 00:05:16.385 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
through the top or the bottom, and

00:05:16.385 --> 00:05:18.253 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the second close still outside.

00:05:18.773 --> 00:05:20.337 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then you stop the bot, which

00:05:20.337 --> 00:05:22.135 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
cancels the waiting orders, and

00:05:22.135 --> 00:05:23.816 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you follow the rule you wrote.

00:05:24.336 --> 00:05:26.124 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write that stop in one sentence.

00:05:27.086 --> 00:05:29.816 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A deposit is crypto or Australian dollars

00:05:29.816 --> 00:05:32.313 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you send into an account at an exchange.

00:05:32.833 --> 00:05:34.849 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An exchange in Australia asks who

00:05:34.849 --> 00:05:36.649 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you are before you can deposit.

00:05:37.169 --> 00:05:39.472 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That check is required by Australian

00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:41.627 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
anti-money laundering law, and the

00:05:41.627 --> 00:05:43.632 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
exchange runs it, not this course.

00:05:44.152 --> 00:05:46.156 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You only upload identification

00:05:46.156 --> 00:05:48.011 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
inside the exchange's own app.

00:05:48.531 --> 00:05:50.598 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This course does not name an exchange

00:05:50.598 --> 00:05:52.162 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and does not show a balance.

00:05:52.423 --> 00:05:54.537 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Before you deposit, look the exchange

00:05:54.537 --> 00:05:56.379 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
up on AUSTRAC's public register.

00:05:56.899 --> 00:05:59.595 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Any exchange offering crypto services in

00:05:59.595 --> 00:06:02.061 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Australia must register with AUSTRAC,

00:06:02.061 --> 00:06:04.680 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Australia's financial crime regulator,

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:06.991 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
as a virtual asset service provider.

00:06:07.511 --> 00:06:08.776 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
AUSTRAC keeps a public

00:06:08.776 --> 00:06:10.117 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
register you can search.

00:06:10.627 --> 00:06:12.806 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Check that register before you sign up.

00:06:13.279 --> 00:06:15.569 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The register says the business is listed.

00:06:15.996 --> 00:06:18.231 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It does not say your money is protected.

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:21.105 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Registration is not a safety guarantee.

00:06:21.625 --> 00:06:23.507 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
ASIC is Australia's financial

00:06:23.507 --> 00:06:24.738 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
services regulator.

00:06:25.258 --> 00:06:27.728 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
From April 2027, new licensing rules

00:06:27.728 --> 00:06:30.116 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
for platforms that hold crypto for

00:06:30.116 --> 00:06:32.504 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you are phased in through that year.

00:06:33.024 --> 00:06:35.035 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Check ASIC for the current position.

00:06:35.163 --> 00:06:37.144 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This lesson names only government

00:06:37.144 --> 00:06:38.596 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bodies, never an exchange.

00:06:39.628 --> 00:06:41.304 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A second code, as well as your

00:06:41.304 --> 00:06:43.742 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
password, is two-factor authentication.

00:06:44.262 --> 00:06:46.363 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Turn that on before any real dollars.

00:06:46.883 --> 00:06:48.916 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then look for a paper or demo mode.

00:06:49.502 --> 00:06:51.024 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Paper uses pretend money.

00:06:51.544 --> 00:06:53.164 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That practice is lesson 7.

00:06:54.214 --> 00:06:56.514 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A fill is an order that actually trades.

00:06:57.034 --> 00:06:59.325 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A maker fee is the charge when your order

00:06:59.325 --> 00:07:01.448 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
waits and someone else trades with it.

00:07:01.658 --> 00:07:03.334 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A taker fee is the charge when

00:07:03.334 --> 00:07:05.066 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your order fills straight away.

00:07:05.402 --> 00:07:07.101 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A grid uses waiting orders,

00:07:07.101 --> 00:07:08.799 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
so read the maker fee first.

00:07:09.319 --> 00:07:10.771 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Some bots also pay a taker

00:07:10.771 --> 00:07:12.224 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
fee when they first start.

00:07:12.633 --> 00:07:15.456 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In this example both are 0.1 percent.

00:07:15.976 --> 00:07:19.055 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
On an example buy of 100 Australian

00:07:19.055 --> 00:07:21.816 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollars, 0.1 percent is 10 cents.

00:07:22.336 --> 00:07:24.459 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The sell costs about 10 cents as well.

00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:26.624 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The round trip is about 20

00:07:26.624 --> 00:07:28.556 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
cents, which is 0.2 percent.

00:07:29.076 --> 00:07:31.114 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This fee row is Australian dollars.

00:07:31.634 --> 00:07:33.589 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is not the summer bitcoin price.

00:07:33.985 --> 00:07:36.297 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the gap is smaller than that 0.2

00:07:36.297 --> 00:07:38.773 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
percent, each completed buy and sell

00:07:38.773 --> 00:07:41.415 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
costs more in fees than the gap is worth.

00:07:41.935 --> 00:07:43.479 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson 5 is where you test

00:07:43.479 --> 00:07:44.803 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a gap against this fee.

00:07:45.323 --> 00:07:47.390 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You do not pick a gap in this lesson.

00:07:48.023 --> 00:07:50.123 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stablecoin is a coin designed

00:07:50.123 --> 00:07:51.819 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
to stay near the value of a

00:07:51.819 --> 00:07:53.838 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
currency such as the US dollar.

00:07:54.358 --> 00:07:55.978 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It can still lose that value.

00:07:56.447 --> 00:07:58.626 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A swap is trading one coin for another.

00:07:59.081 --> 00:08:01.069 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the price is in a stablecoin,

00:08:01.069 --> 00:08:02.341 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
every fill is a swap.

00:08:03.391 --> 00:08:05.140 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A trading journal is a dated

00:08:05.140 --> 00:08:07.117 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
record of every bot: the plan, the

00:08:07.117 --> 00:08:08.866 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
changes, the fills, the fees, a

00:08:08.866 --> 00:08:10.919 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
review note of what happened, and

00:08:10.919 --> 00:08:12.896 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
whether you followed the rules.

00:08:13.416 --> 00:08:15.204 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That note is not money you made.

00:08:15.553 --> 00:08:17.687 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stablecoin fill goes in the journal.

00:08:18.207 --> 00:08:20.239 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is also the page you will open

00:08:20.239 --> 00:08:22.192 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
again in lesson 8 and lesson 10.

00:08:22.712 --> 00:08:25.238 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
For every transaction, including a buy,

00:08:25.238 --> 00:08:27.526 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a sell, a swap, or a transfer, write the

00:08:27.526 --> 00:08:29.894 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
date and time, the amount, the value in

00:08:29.894 --> 00:08:32.420 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Australian dollars at the time, the fee,

00:08:32.420 --> 00:08:34.787 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
which exchange or wallet, what it was

00:08:34.787 --> 00:08:36.681 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
for, and who the other side was.

00:08:37.201 --> 00:08:39.259 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The columns are the date, the pair,

00:08:39.259 --> 00:08:41.087 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the band, the gaps, the money in

00:08:41.087 --> 00:08:42.992 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the bot, the stop rule, the fills,

00:08:42.992 --> 00:08:44.973 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the fees, the Australian dollar

00:08:44.973 --> 00:08:46.954 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
value of each fill, a review note,

00:08:46.954 --> 00:08:48.630 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and a yes or no for the rules.

00:08:49.150 --> 00:08:51.253 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Download your exchange's transaction

00:08:51.253 --> 00:08:53.264 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
history at least every three months.

00:08:53.686 --> 00:08:54.915 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Keep those records for

00:08:54.915 --> 00:08:56.032 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
at least five years.

00:08:56.388 --> 00:08:58.160 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is general information,

00:08:58.160 --> 00:08:59.046 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
not tax advice.

00:08:59.566 --> 00:09:01.354 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Leave two columns blank for now.

00:09:01.773 --> 00:09:02.936 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
One is for the fees.

00:09:03.456 --> 00:09:05.747 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
One is for whether you followed the rule.

00:09:05.881 --> 00:09:07.054 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You fill those later.

00:09:07.503 --> 00:09:09.347 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You do not fill them with a hope.

00:09:10.008 --> 00:09:12.007 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Nobody from this course will

00:09:12.007 --> 00:09:13.507 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
ask for a seed phrase, a

00:09:13.507 --> 00:09:15.424 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
private key, or an API secret.

00:09:15.944 --> 00:09:18.552 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a message rushes you to send crypto, or

00:09:18.552 --> 00:09:21.002 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
asks for one of those, treat it as a scam.

00:09:21.522 --> 00:09:22.751 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is not this course.

00:09:23.763 --> 00:09:26.215 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
ASIC's Moneysmart website is the public

00:09:26.215 --> 00:09:28.378 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Australian guide for scam warnings.

00:09:28.899 --> 00:09:29.904 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Check it yourself.

00:09:30.895 --> 00:09:32.962 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Say the page once, in your own words,

00:09:32.962 --> 00:09:34.749 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and do not read the chart again.

00:09:34.999 --> 00:09:36.899 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Name the pair, the band, the gaps,

00:09:36.899 --> 00:09:38.570 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the stop rule, then stop.

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:41.209 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a word on it has not been defined,

00:09:41.209 --> 00:09:43.329 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
stop and define it before you go on.

00:09:43.849 --> 00:09:45.771 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A secret is a seed phrase, a

00:09:45.771 --> 00:09:47.876 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
private key, or an API secret.

00:09:48.396 --> 00:09:50.072 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
None of those go on this page.

00:09:50.470 --> 00:09:52.148 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You write Example on your own

00:09:52.148 --> 00:09:54.036 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
notebook so a practice sketch is

00:09:54.036 --> 00:09:56.133 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
never later mistaken for a live plan.

00:09:57.183 --> 00:09:59.563 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Recap: your page has seven items, each

00:09:59.563 --> 00:10:01.704 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
with a written fact, every figure

00:10:01.704 --> 00:10:04.005 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
marked Example, and no secrets on it.

00:10:05.205 --> 00:10:07.187 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Next lesson: What is a grid bot.

00:10:07.707 --> 00:10:09.271 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Bring your notes: your band,

00:10:09.271 --> 00:10:10.891 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your gaps and your stop rule.

00:10:11.164 --> 00:10:12.522 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Keep the word Example on

00:10:12.522 --> 00:10:13.812 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
every practice figure.

00:10:14.332 --> 00:10:15.980 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Next lesson you will see what

00:10:15.980 --> 00:10:17.600 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the bot does, order by order.

